.TH qsh-setup-client 1  "client 0.4.2" 
.SH NAME
qsh\-setup\-client \- This machine connects to a host with `qsh <name>`
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBqsh setup client\fR [\fB\-\-address\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-code\-stdin\fR] [\fB\-\-jsonl\fR] [\fB\-\-peer\-cert\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fINAME\fR] [\fICODE\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
This machine connects to a host with `qsh <name>`
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-address\fR \fI<ADDR>\fR
`host:port` of the host
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit a single `qsh.cli/v1` JSON envelope on stdout instead of human\-readable text
.TP
\fB\-\-code\-stdin\fR
Read the invite code from standard input
.TP
\fB\-\-jsonl\fR
Emit newline\-delimited JSON on stdout (reserved for streaming commands; non\-streaming commands emit a single line, same as `\-\-json`)
.TP
\fB\-\-peer\-cert\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Pin the host from its certificate file (`\-` reads standard input) instead of redeeming an invite
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase diagnostic verbosity on stderr (`\-v` info, `\-vv` debug, `\-vvv` trace). Never affects stdout (`docs/CLI.md` §2.2)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress diagnostic output on stderr
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
[\fINAME\fR]
The name to pin the host under
.TP
[\fICODE\fR]
The invite code the host printed. With no code, no `\-\-code\-stdin` and no `\-\-peer\-cert`, a terminal is prompted with echo off
.SH VERSION
v0.4.2
